{"anchor": {"begin": [1, 0, 632.12], "end": [1, 0, 641.82], "file": "toy.tex", "kind": "approximate", "line": 75}, "blockers": [], "class": "out-of-scope", "clauses": [], "context_tex": "\\begin{proof}\nFix $n$. By Theorem~\\ref{thm:triangle},\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:bound-sum}\n  2\\,T_n = n^2 + n.\n\\end{equation}\nFor every natural number $k \\ge 0$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:bound-range}\n  n \\le k\\,n^2,\n\\end{equation}\nand the choice $k = 1$ in \\eqref{eq:bound-range} gives $2T_n \\le 2n^2$, so $C = 1$ works.", "decls": {"Toy.Acceptance.thm_bound": "61b409959aae9417dafe7493", "Toy.PaperSpec.thm_bound": "5c9beeb3df8f78a5fe479560", "Toy.triangle": "21bf5b5befd073f5ae09a227", "Toy.triangle._f": "5094cac6869860b2b8305b6e", "Toy.triangle.match_1": "c2932abc2461598d920667a6"}, "findings": [], "id": "T:eq:bound-range", "kind": "equation", "location": "toy.tex:75", "number": "Equation (3)", "paper": "T", "parent": "T:thm:bound", "release": "r-be409c640640", "schema": "prooflens/manifest@1", "scope": "proof-step", "scope_note": "a step of the proof of Theorem 2.5", "scope_reviewed": true, "source_evidence": {"placement": "approximate", "state": "pass"}, "source_matches": true, "source_sha256": "4640c8e3da3aba8d9a9e58abd761bf9c41ec8d0bafd25609f0d143cf9f3e62ef", "statement_tex": "For every natural number $k \\ge 0$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:bound-range}\n  n \\le k\\,n^2,\n\\end{equation}", "status": "out of scope: proof-step", "status_code": "scope.proof-step", "step": {"correspondence": null, "links": [], "parent": {"file": "T_thm_bound-c82142db.json", "heading": null, "id": "T:thm:bound", "number": "Theorem 2.5", "title": "Uniform bound"}, "review": {"finding": {"comparison": "At k = 0 and n = 1 the step reads 1 <= 0, which is false. For k >= 1 it holds, since n <= n^2 <= k n^2. The proof uses k = 1 only, so restricting the range to k >= 1 repairs the step and the enclosing result is unaffected.", "current": true, "locked_at": "2026-10-19T12:00:00Z", "project_commit": null, "reading": "For every natural number k with k >= 0 and every natural number n (n fixed at the start of the proof), the step asserts n <= k n^2. The proof then uses only k = 1.", "release": null, "reviewer": {"id": "human:A-Referee", "identity": "self-declared", "kind": "human", "model": null, "name": "A Referee", "same_family_as_author": "no"}, "source_sha256": "4640c8e3da3aba8d9a9e58abd761bf9c41ec8d0bafd25609f0d143cf9f3e62ef", "state": "false", "submitted_at": "2026-10-19T12:06:00Z", "verdict": {"detail": "The printed range k >= 0 fails at k = 0, n = 1 (1 <= 0). The step holds for every k >= 1, and the next line uses k = 1.", "group": "problem", "value": "false as printed"}}, "reports": [{"comparison": "At k = 0 and n = 1 the step reads 1 <= 0, which is false. For k >= 1 it holds, since n <= n^2 <= k n^2. The proof uses k = 1 only, so restricting the range to k >= 1 repairs the step and the enclosing result is unaffected.", "current": true, "locked_at": "2026-10-19T12:00:00Z", "project_commit": null, "reading": "For every natural number k with k >= 0 and every natural number n (n fixed at the start of the proof), the step asserts n <= k n^2. The proof then uses only k = 1.", "release": null, "reviewer": {"id": "human:A-Referee", "identity": "self-declared", "kind": "human", "model": null, "name": "A Referee", "same_family_as_author": "no"}, "source_sha256": "4640c8e3da3aba8d9a9e58abd761bf9c41ec8d0bafd25609f0d143cf9f3e62ef", "state": "false", "submitted_at": "2026-10-19T12:06:00Z", "verdict": {"detail": "The printed range k >= 0 fails at k = 0, n = 1 (1 <= 0). The step holds for every k >= 1, and the next line uses k = 1.", "group": "problem", "value": "false as printed"}}], "state": "false"}, "route": {"by": "human:A-Referee", "links": [{"axioms": ["propext", "Quot.sound"], "class": "proved", "doc": null, "errors": [], "fingerprint": "pl-fp-v1:e7dee0b4bc55a112174c3361f731a3e5e32c1ffdf6055a8ddb1f599a204bc2b6", "kind": "theorem", "module": "Toy.